// The names still dispatched by the WORLD_PAIRED table take an array or a MutableArray and
// nothing else, and the message says what each world answers with rather than only naming the
// type it was handed.
//
// This used to call `sort`, which F178 converted into a real overload set -- so `sort` no longer
// reaches this message at all, and asserting it here would have pinned the table by a name that
// had left it. `reverse` is still in the table; `overload_no_candidate_rejected` holds the other
// half of the pair, which is what `sort(Set)` says now.
fn main() {
    print(reverse(Set<int> { 1, 2 }))
}
